            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac syncope secondary to glossopharyngeal neuralgia--effectively treated with carbamazepine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>776-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 64-year-old male with glossopharyngeal neuralgia, cardiac asystole and grand mal seizures has been relieved of his attacks by intake of 400 mg of Carbamazepine per day over a 4-year period. Simultaneous EEG-EKG recordings before and after drinking water document the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
